Looking at this problem, I need to analyze the lemma bodies in HelperA.dfy and HelperB.dfy to understand why verification might be failing.

The key insight is that `K.Override(m,n)` gives priority to `n` over `m` - when a key exists in both, the value from `n` is used. So:
- `Override(m,n)[q] == if q in n then n[q] else m[q]`

In the forall block, I need to prove that `left[q] == right[q]` where:
- `left = Restrict(Override(m,n), keep)`
- `right = Override(Restrict(m,keep), Restrict(n,keep))`

For a key `q` in `left`:
- `left[q] = Override(m,n)[q] = if q in n then n[q] else m[q]`
- `right[q] = if q in rn then rn[q] else rm[q] = if q in n && q in keep then n[q] else (if q in m && q in keep then m[q] else ...)`

Since `q in left` means `q in merged && q in keep`, and `merged.Keys == m.Keys + n.Keys`, we have `q in keep` and `(q in m || q in n)`.

The issue in the original code is the condition check - it checks `if q in m` but should check `if q in n` since Override gives priority to `n`.

Let me fix the logic:

```json
{
  "HelperA.dfy": "var merged := K.Override(m,n);
    var left := K.Restrict(merged,keep);
    var rm := K.Restrict(m,keep);
    var rn := K.Restrict(n,keep);
    var right := K.Override(rm,rn);
    D.OverrideKeys(m,n);
    D.RestrictKeys(merged,keep);
    D.RestrictKeys(m,keep);
    D.RestrictKeys(n,keep);
    D.OverrideKeys(rm,rn);
    assert left.Keys == right.Keys;
    forall q | q in left ensures q in right && left[q] == right[q] {
      V.RestrictAt(merged,keep,q);
      V.OverrideAt(m,n,q);
      if q in n {
        V.RestrictAt(n,keep,q);
      } else {
        V.RestrictAt(m,keep,q);
      }
      V.OverrideAt(rm,rn,q);
    }
    A.Equal(left,right);",
  "HelperB.dfy": "var merged := K.Override(m,n);
    var left := K.Restrict(merged,keep);
    var rm := K.Restrict(m,keep);
    var rn := K.Restrict(n,keep);
    var right := K.Override(rm,rn);
    D.OverrideKeys(m,n);
    D.RestrictKeys(merged,keep);
    D.RestrictKeys(m,keep);
    D.RestrictKeys(n,keep);
    D.OverrideKeys(rm,rn);
    assert left.Keys == right.Keys;
    forall q | q in left ensures q in right && left[q] == right[q] {
      V.RestrictAt(merged,keep,q);
      V.OverrideAt(m,n,q);
      if q in n {
        V.RestrictAt(n,keep,q);
      } else {
        V.RestrictAt(m,keep,q);
      }
      V.OverrideAt(rm,rn,q);
    }
    A.Equal(left,right);"
}
```

